// Dev container: a ready environment with nothing to install on your machine. Works the same on Windows, macOS and Linux.
//   GitHub:  Code -> Codespaces -> Create codespace on main
//   VS Code: install "Dev Containers", then "Reopen in Container" (needs Docker)
// It runs `bash scripts/setup.sh --all` once when the container is created (Node 22, npm packages, Z3, Rust, cargo-near,
// Java + TLA+); the base image allows sudo without a password, so nothing prompts. Then: npm test, npm run demo
// (then open port 8080 from the Ports tab), npm run verify, npm run test:rust.
//
// Tested (2026-11-14) on GitHub Codespaces (2 cores): the container built and `setup.sh --all` finished without prompts
// (Node 22.23.5, Z3 5.4.1, Rust 1.100.0, cargo-near 0.23.0, OpenJDK 17); `npm run doctor` all green except ffmpeg
// (maintainers only). npm test, test:e2e, verify, test:rust and demo passed. Not yet tested: VS Code with local Docker.
//
// Port 8080 only notifies, it doesn't open a browser: the test scripts (npm run test:e2e and others) start and stop a
// server on 8080, and a page opened automatically would load after it has gone and show no recipes.
{
  "name": "Sealed Recipes",
  "image": "mcr.microsoft.com/devcontainers/base:ubuntu-24.04",
  "postCreateCommand": "bash scripts/setup.sh --all",
  "forwardPorts": [8080, 8787],
  "portsAttributes": {
    "8080": { "label": "demo (marketplace + app)", "onAutoForward": "notify" },
    "8787": { "label": "runner", "onAutoForward": "silent" }
  },
  "hostRequirements": { "cpus": 2, "memory": "4gb" },
  "customizations": {
    "vscode": { "extensions": ["rust-lang.rust-analyzer"] }
  }
}
